cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite the exact repository commit and the QRH route paper. The authors are
  the project owner bernkastel299792458 and the AI systems Codex and Claude,
  credited at the project owner's direction. See AI_USE.md for actual contributions and
  LICENSE for per-material terms: original code uses 0BSD, original text/data
  use CC0-1.0, and third-party files retain their own licenses.
title: "Primes between consecutive sixth powers: an explicit conditional proof and Lean formalization"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "bernkastel299792458 (project owner)"
  - name: "Codex (OpenAI; QRH route lead, AI system)"
  - name: "Claude (Anthropic; early-version reviewer, AI system)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bernkastel299792458/legendre-kth-powers"
url: "https://github.com/bernkastel299792458/legendre-kth-powers/tree/main/routes/qrh"
abstract: >-
  A complete downstream Lean proof of a prime strictly between consecutive
  sixth powers for every positive integer, relative to seven named external
  inputs: QRH(7/8), CS v2, Rosser zero counting, an integrated explicit
  formula, finite-height RH, CHJII short intervals, and twelve CHL rows.
  The repository includes a readable Chinese paper, source provenance,
  exact rational certificates, proof sources and recorded verification.
keywords:
  - number theory
  - primes in short intervals
  - Lean
  - conditional proof
